Psycho is a classic.

Wonderfully shot, amazing atmosphere and an incredible ending. Also love the use of symbolism through the crows and mirrors throughout the film.

Its interesting how Norman always looks like he's looking beyond something, like he's not actually present (which ends up being great foreshadowing for the twist). He's always covered by a shadow, or off center, like the shot in his office with Marion where one half of the shot is the owl in the background, or the scene with the detective, where he sits on the right side of the window sill.

Makes it all the more perfect when the final scene is him looking directly into the camera, perfectly centered. Alluding to the idea that he is no longer split, but completely one now.

Fantastic movie.
